\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

CNV streamliner. The aim of this package is to streamline the analysis of results produced by CNV tools. It introduces the cnvstrml object and parsers for commonly used methods. Inputs: It has some methods to compare different calls. Available support for FACETS, PureCN, SCLUST, Sequenza, GATK CopyNumber, ControlFreec (without subclones), Battenberg, CNVkit, SEG (Generic input file for IGV). Outputs: VCF (v4.2 compliant), SEG, GISTIC2.0 segment files. Visualization: This package contains methods to visualize the segments of a genome or of a choromosme or a cohort of samples Metrics: It also provides metrics for the segmentation result and allows to compare CNV calls among samples using standard CNV metrics. Using the CNAQC package it provides a PASS/FAIL result for the sample and for each segment.
